  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Widespread precipitation today with mountain snow.\n\n- Active weather pattern through at least mid next week.\n\n\nTwo disturbances will be colliding over the Northern Rockies\ntoday. A low pressure system that is over the Great Basin region\nand a trough of low pressure moving into the Pacific Northwest.\nThese disturbances will be bringing widespread precipitation to\nthe region along with causing cooler temperatures. The bulk of the\nprecipitation is expected to fall across west central down into\nsouthwest Montana. Snow levels are expected to fall to around 5000\nfeet by this evening causing accumulating snow to Lemhi county and\nsouthwest Montana. The most impactful snow is expected along the\nContinental Divide around Butte, so a winter weather advisory has\nbeen issued. \n\nThe region will experience a short break in the precipitation late\nSaturday into Sunday as a transitory ridge slides over the region,\nbut another low pressure system is expected to push into the\nPacific Northwest by Monday. The models diverge on how this low\nwill track over the western United States, but the region should\nanticipated seasonal temperatures along with occasional\nprecipitation through at least mid next week.",
